This repository is a hard fork of duckdb/duckdb-rs (tag v1.20000.0, which
corresponds to the DuckDB 2.0.0 engine). The upstream MIT LICENSE is preserved
verbatim. Modifications introduced by Haybarn:

  - Published crate names renamed:
      duckdb                -> haybarn
      libduckdb-sys         -> libhaybarn-sys
      duckdb-loadable-macros -> haybarn-loadable-macros
      duckdb-neo            -> haybarn-neo
    The on-disk crate directories under crates/ keep their upstream names so the
    Haybarn changes remain a thin, rebasable stack on top of the upstream tag.

  - The wrapper crates' library names are `haybarn` and `haybarn_neo`. The C API, the
    `duckdb::` C++ namespace, the public headers (duckdb.h / duckdb.hpp), and the
    DUCKDB_VERSION macro are preserved verbatim — Haybarn is intentionally
    ABI-compatible with DuckDB.

  - The sys crate's `links` key is renamed from "duckdb" to "haybarn" so the
    crate can coexist in a dependency graph with the upstream libduckdb-sys.
    Downstream build scripts read DEP_HAYBARN_* instead of DEP_DUCKDB_*.

  - haybarn-loadable-macros emits `::haybarn::ffi` and `::haybarn_neo::` paths
    (renamed from `::duckdb::ffi` and `::duckdb_neo::`).

  - The bundled sources (crates/libduckdb-sys/duckdb.tar.gz) are regenerated
    from the Haybarn engine via the duckdb-sources submodule, which is re-pointed
    at Query-farm-haybarn/haybarn, and stamped with the release version (v2.0.0)
    rather than a -dev version. As a result the bundled build embeds the single
    Haybarn RSA extension trust root (for both core and community extensions)
    and the haybarn-extensions.query.farm repository URLs. DuckDB-signed
    extensions will not load.

  - Linked mode downloads Haybarn's prebuilt libhaybarn-<platform>.zip from the
    Query-farm-haybarn/haybarn GitHub release pinned in
    crates/libduckdb-sys/.duckdb-release (never DuckDB's binaries), and links
    `haybarn` / `haybarn_static`; pkg-config and vcpkg probe `haybarn`.

  - Upstream's GitHub workflows are replaced by Haybarn CI and a crates.io
    Trusted Publishing workflow.

  - READMEs rebranded; duck-themed branding and examples removed.

Source for the underlying Haybarn engine (DuckDB as modified by Haybarn) is at:
https://github.com/Query-farm-haybarn/haybarn

The original duckdb-rs project lives at:
https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb-rs
